{
  "description": "Targets of rig_transfer.py: the characters of Silent Hill by the name of their model file (convert/models/CHARA/<NAME>.glb; print a skeleton with --inspect NAME). mode 'rig': 'roles' give the game bone (NN of boneNN) of every body part the skeleton has, a part without a bone follows the part above it, and 'proportions' says whose bone lengths the result has -- 'source' (the people-shaped characters): the model keeps its own proportions at one scale ('scale': a number instead of the scale that matches the target's stature, 'scale_factor': a factor on it) and the glb carries its own rest pose, which the engine plays the character's clips on; 'target' (the default; animals and other shapes): every limb is stretched onto the target's bone; mode 'chain': the body is bent along the listed bones, feet first; mode 'blob': the body is fitted into the creature's box ('up' and 'front': where the source's head and face point, in the glb's axes) and takes its weights from the original mesh. 'pose' turns parts of the source before the fit: {role: [axis, degrees]}.",
